# `core.autocrlf=true` on a Windows checkout rewrites text files to CRLF. For
# most of this repository that is invisible. For a file the container executes
# it is not: a `#!/bin/sh` line ending in CR makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r", and the container dies with
# "no such file or directory" naming a path that plainly exists.
#
# Scoped deliberately narrowly. A blanket `* text=auto` would renormalise every
# file in the repository on the next commit, burying a real change in a diff
# nobody can read.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
